<title>USA: US inflation protected bonds opposed by Rep Archer.</title>
<headline>US inflation protected bonds opposed by Rep Archer.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>House Ways and Means Chairman Bill Archer said Wednesday he opposed the Clinton administration's plans to issue Treasury bonds which guarantee an interest rate above the inflation rate next year.</p>
<p>&quot;It plays Russian roulette with the debt service charges of the federal budget,&quot; Archer, R-Texas, told reporters. &quot;You don't know what inflation will be and you can't predict what your debt service charges will be in the future.&quot;</p>
<p>Archer said the Treasury may have the legal authority to issue the bonds, but he hoped it would not do so. He said he would hold hearings on the proposal early next year.</p>
</text>
